From 0e4a0260d2015b083fe9cbabd4482ae713404a34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Axis wiring session)" <dawn@regentplatform.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:56:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Design system overhaul + restore lost Phase 1
 balance/error-state work
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DESIGN SYSTEM ("Institutional Ledger")
Deliberately moves away from generic SaaS blue toward something reading
as serious business/accounting software, per direction: professional,
not "SaaSy."

- app/globals.css: new HSL token set — deep navy primary, muted
  forest-teal accent (success states), brick red (not alarm-red) for
  destructive, warm off-white background. Headings use font-display.
- app/layout.tsx: added Source Serif 4 (headings — signals a tool built
  for keeping books, not a consumer app) and JetBrains Mono (all monetary
  figures, tabular convention) alongside existing Inter. Also fixed
  metadata still describing Axis as a "QuickBooks alternative" / tagged
  "SaaS" — leftover from before the done-for-you repositioning.
- tailwind.config.ts: remapped axis.blue/green/red/gray/light to
  reference the new CSS variables instead of hardcoded hex. Every
  existing bg-axis-blue etc. usage across the app picks up the new
  palette automatically — this is why most files below show as modified
  despite no logic changes, only a global hover-color fix (see below).
- Global fix: hover:bg-blue-800 (Tailwind's default blue, disconnected
  from the new navy token) was hardcoded identically in 19 files, always
  paired with bg-axis-blue. Replaced with hover:bg-axis-blue-light
  everywhere so hover states stay in sync with the token system.

SHARED COMPONENTS
- components/shared/PageHeader.tsx (new): replaces the near-identical
  hand-rolled title/description/actions header block that was previously
  duplicated with slightly different markup across 6 pages.
- components/shared/StatusBadge.tsx (new): consistent status styling
  (invoice, journal entry, employee statuses) replacing three different
  ad-hoc badge-coloring approaches across Ledger, Transactions, and
  Invoices.
- components/dashboard/StatCard.tsx: stat values now use font-mono for
  tabular alignment.

REGRESSION FIX: restored work lost from an earlier, never-actually-merged
patch (confirmed via git log — only the original wiring patch landed,
a later "Phase 1 complete" patch did not, apparently lost in local
patch-file mixups on a prior session):
- lib/finance/balance.ts (recreated): the computeAccountBalance double-
  entry balance calculation.
- components/shared/TableErrorState.tsx (recreated): distinguishes a
  failed fetch from genuinely empty data.
- BankingView, AccountsList: real computed balances restored (had
  silently reverted to a hardcoded 0.00 / placeholder "—").
- LedgerView, TransactionsView, ClientsList, InvoicesList: isError/
  refetch + TableErrorState restored.
- ClientsList, InvoicesList, AccountsList: the silent
  `{currentOrg && <Form />}` pattern (renders nothing with no
  explanation if org is missing) replaced with a visible fallback
  message, matching the fix already applied to Ledger/Transactions/
  Banking in an earlier session.
- InvoicesList: also fixed a real currency bug found while restoring
  this file — amounts were hardcoded with a literal "$" regardless of
  invoice.currency (wrong for a UGX-based business).

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean on every touched file.
Production build not verified in this sandbox (no network access to
Google Fonts here — confirmed unrelated to code correctness in prior
sessions the same way).
